          },
          "children" : [ {
            "children" : [ {
              "attributes" : {
                "dxpStyle" : { },
                "imageInfos" : "",
                "richTextValue" : "<h1>Woods-Grown American Ginseng</h1>\n<p>Woods-grown ginseng is a cultivation method that mimics the natural growing conditions of wild American ginseng \n    (Panax quinquefolius L.). This approach involves planting ginseng seeds in forested areas, allowing the \n    plants to grow under the natural canopy and soil conditions typically found in the wild. Unlike cultivated \n    ginseng, which is often grown in open fields under artificial shade cloth with controlled conditions, \n    wild-simulated ginseng benefits from the natural ecosystem and is still cared for and tended to. \n    It usually takes about 5 to 10 years for it to reach maturity.</p>"
              },
              "definition" : "community_builder:htmlEditor",
              "id" : "1f9898dd-233c-4036-adbf-cc383ce4d953",
              "type" : "component"
            } ],
