          },
          "children" : [ {
            "children" : [ {
              "attributes" : {
                "dxpStyle" : { },
                "imageInfos" : "",
                "richTextValue" : "<h1>Bird's Nest</h1>\n\n<p>When prepared correctly, bird’s nests are a rare delicacy renowned as a source of unprocessed collagen to naturally enhance your beauty. Hsu’s bird's nests are created from the saliva of a small bird called the edible-nest swiftlet (Aerodramus fuciphagus). They are considered a symbol of wealth, good health, and status. In Asian culture, women will drink bird's nest together to indulge in the rich nutrients that enhance skin health. \n<br><br>\n\n\n    <strong>White</strong>: Nests are originally white in color and are the most common type of bird's nest. They are normally harvested from eaves of roofs, human-constructed houses specifically built to encourage nest building or wherever the swiftlet decides to build its nest.\n<br><br>\n\n\n    <strong>Gold</strong>: When the sun hits the nest, and special conditions are just right during the drying process, a golden hue emerges. The golden color is more prized due to its rarity and color.\n<br><br>\n\n\n    <strong>Cave</strong>: In the wild, cave nests are harvested from natural geologically formed caves that are exposed to minerals from the cave walls. They are typically darker in color, more difficult to obtain and are labor-intensive to harvest.</p>"
              },
              "definition" : "community_builder:htmlEditor",
              "id" : "e6bfdb51-6a94-48b1-b20b-360e2c355e10",
              "type" : "component"
            } ],
