          "children" : [ {
            "children" : [ {
              "attributes" : {
                "dxpStyle" : { },
                "imageInfos" : "",
                "richTextValue" : "<h1>Hokkaido Scallops</h1>\n\n<p>Hokkaido scallops are a species of scallops native to the cold, \n    northern waters surrounding the most northerly island of Japan, \n    near the territorial waters of Russia. At Hsu’s Ginseng, we \n    source our scallops directly from Hokkaido, Japan, where 80% \n    are farmed in the Sea of Okhotsk. The waters in this \n    region are rich in nutrients and are home to a variety of marine \n    life. Like ginseng, the scallop beds of Hokkaido are also located at 45° N latitude.</p>"
              },
              "definition" : "community_builder:htmlEditor",
              "id" : "6646126d-8106-4ae1-8c48-5368e5931011",
              "type" : "component"
